    "topic": "Four Operations",
    "question": "Ken and Ivan had some sweets. After Ken gave away 5/7 of his sweets, he had 2/3 as many sweets as Ivan. Ivan then gave away 120 sweets and he had 1/4 as many sweets as Ken. How many sweets did each of them have at 1st?",
    "answer": "Ivan: 144 sweets; Ken: 336 sweets",
    "model": "bar-change",
    "hint": "Use the 1st condition to relate Ken's remaining 2 parts to Ivan's 3 parts. Then use Ivan's 120-sweet change and the 1:4 comparison.",
    "solution": {
      "en": {
        "strategy": "Relate Ken's remaining sweets to Ivan's sweets, then use Ivan's 120-sweet loss.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Set up the first comparison",
            "text": "Ken kept 2/7 of his original sweets, and this was 2/3 as many as Ivan's amount. Thus Ken's remaining sweets : Ivan's sweets = 2 : 3."
          },
          {
            "title": "Use Ivan's later amount",
            "text": "Let Ken's remaining amount be 4 units. Ivan's original amount is then 6 units. After Ivan gives away 120 sweets, he has 1 unit because he has 1/4 as many as Ken's 4 units. Therefore 5 units = 120, so 1 unit = 24."
          },
          {
            "title": "Work back to both starting amounts",
            "text": "Ivan had 6 × 24 = 144 sweets. Ken had 4 × 24 = 96 sweets after giving away 5/7, which is 2/7 of his original amount. Ken originally had 96 × 7 ÷ 2 = 336 sweets."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "Ivan: 144 sweets; Ken: 336 sweets"
      },
      "zh-Hans": {
        "strategy": "先把Ken剩下的糖果和Ivan的糖果建立比例，再利用Ivan送出120颗糖果。",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "建立第1个比例",
            "text": "Ken剩下原来糖果的2/7，而这相当于Ivan糖果的2/3。因此Ken剩下的糖果 : Ivan原有的糖果 = 2 : 3。"
          },
          {
            "title": "利用Ivan后来剩下的数量",
            "text": "把Ken剩下的糖果设为4份，Ivan原有的是6份。Ivan送出120颗后只剩1份，因为这时Ivan的糖果是Ken的4份的1/4。于是5份 = 120，1份 = 24。"
          },
          {
            "title": "倒推开始时的数量",
            "text": "Ivan原有6 × 24 = 144颗糖果。Ken送出后有4 × 24 = 96颗，这占原有数量的2/7，所以Ken原有96 × 7 ÷ 2 = 336颗糖果。"
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "Ivan原有144颗糖果；Ken原有336颗糖果。"
      }
    },
