    "id": 51,
    "topic": "Measurement",
    "question": "Jessica spent 2/3 of her money on a book and a toy. Don spent 1/5 of his money on the same items. The book cost $18 and the toy cost $6 less. How much more money did Don have than Jessica at first?",
    "answer": "$105",
    "model": "fraction-of-remainder",
    "hint": "First find the cost of the book and toy together. Treat that same cost as 2/3 of Jessica's money and 1/5 of Don's money.",
    "solution": {
      "en": {
        "strategy": "Find the common cost of the book and toy, then treat it as 2/3 of Jessica's money and 1/5 of Don's money.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Find the cost of both items",
            "text": "The toy costs $18 − $6 = $12. Together, the book and toy cost $18 + $12 = $30."
          },
          {
            "title": "Find each starting amount",
            "text": "For Jessica, $30 is 2/3 of her money, so she had $30 ÷ 2 × 3 = $45. For Don, $30 is 1/5 of his money, so he had $30 × 5 = $150."
          },
          {
            "title": "Find the difference",
            "text": "Don had $150 − $45 = $105 more than Jessica."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "The checked difference in their initial money is $105."
      },
      "zh-Hans": {
        "strategy": "先求书和玩具的共同价格，再把它分别看作Jessica钱的2/3和Don钱的1/5。",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "求2件物品的价格",
            "text": "玩具价格是$18 − $6 = $12。书和玩具共$18 + $12 = $30。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求原有金额",
            "text": "对Jessica，$30是她钱的2/3，所以她有$30 ÷ 2 × 3 = $45。对Don，$30是他钱的1/5，所以他有$30 × 5 = $150。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求差额",
            "text": "Don比Jessica多$150 − $45 = $105。"
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "答案：Don原来比Jessica多$105。"
      }
    },
