    "id": 56,
    "topic": "Ratio",
    "question": "There were 980 pears and oranges in a basket. After 1/3 of the pears and 230 oranges were sold, the ratio of pears to oranges left was 2 : 3. What was the ratio of pears to oranges at first?",
    "answer": "75 : 121",
    "model": "fraction-of-remainder",
    "hint": "Represent the remaining pears and oranges with a 2 : 3 bar. Restore the 1/3 of pears and the 230 oranges that were sold.",
    "solution": {
      "en": {
        "strategy": "Use the final 2 : 3 ratio to relate the original pear and orange totals.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Set up the final ratio",
            "text": "Let the original amounts be P pears and O oranges. Then (2/3P) : (O − 230) = 2 : 3, so 2P = 2(O − 230), or P = O − 230."
          },
          {
            "title": "Use the total",
            "text": "P + O = 980 gives (O − 230) + O = 980. Thus O = 605 and P = 375, so P : O = 375 : 605 = 75 : 121."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "The ratio of pears to oranges at first was 75 : 121."
      },
      "zh-Hans": {
        "strategy": "用最后的 2 : 3 比关联原来梨和橙子的数量。",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "列出最后的比",
            "text": "设原来有 P 个梨和 O 个橙子。则 (2/3P) : (O − 230) = 2 : 3，所以 2P = 2(O − 230)，即 P = O − 230。"
          },
          {
            "title": "使用总数",
            "text": "P + O = 980，所以 (O − 230) + O = 980。得到 O = 605，P = 375，因此 P : O = 375 : 605 = 75 : 121。"
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "起初梨和橙子的比是 75 : 121。"
      }
    },
