        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Find the small rectangle",
            "text": "Its dimensions are 26 − 4 − 4 = 18 m and 19 − 2 − 2 = 15 m, so its area is 18 × 15 = 270 m2."
          },
          {
            "title": "Compare the areas",
            "text": "Using PQ : BC = 5 : 3 for the similar triangles shown gives a total shaded area of 216 m2. Therefore shaded : small rectangle = 216 : 270 = 4 : 5."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "The shaded portion to the small rectangle is 4 : 5."
