          {
            "title": "Find the vertex angle of triangle BPQ",
            "text": "At B, ∠PBC = 90° − 40° − 42° = 8°. Therefore ∠PBQ = 8° + 54° = 62°."
          },
          {
            "title": "Use the isosceles triangle",
            "text": "BP = BQ, so the 2 base angles are equal. Each is (180° − 62°) ÷ 2."
          }
