    "id": 86,
    "topic": "2-part: Measurement",
    "question": "Cleo wanted to buy 16 similarly priced T-shirts but was $8 short. If she had bought 7 such T-shirts instead, she would have $19 left. (a) What was the cost of 2 such T-shirts? (b) How much money did Cleo have?",
    "answer": "(a) $6; (b) $40",
    "model": "money-units",
    "hint": "Compare the 16-shirt and 7-shirt situations. The difference of 9 shirts accounts for both the $8 shortage and the $19 left.",
    "solution": {
      "en": {
        "strategy": "Compare the two possible purchases so that the same amount of Cleo's money is represented twice.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Match the two situations",
            "text": "For 16 T-shirts, Cleo needs $8 more, so her money is 16 shirt-prices minus $8. For 7 T-shirts, she has $19 left, so her money is 7 shirt-prices plus $19."
          },
          {
            "title": "Find one shirt price",
            "text": "The difference is 16 - 7 = 9 T-shirts, and the money difference is $8 + $19 = $27. So 9 T-shirts cost $27, and 1 T-shirt costs $3."
          },
          {
            "title": "Answer both parts",
            "text": "2 T-shirts cost 2 × $3 = $6. Cleo had 7 × $3 + $19 = $40."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "Check: (a) $6; (b) $40"
      },
      "zh-Hans": {
        "strategy": "比较 2 种购买情况，把 Cleo 的相同金额用 2 个式子表示。",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "对应 2 种情况",
            "text": "买 16 件 T 恤时还差 $8，所以她的钱是 16 件的价钱减 $8。买 7 件 T 恤时余下 $19，所以她的钱是 7 件的价钱加 $19。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求每件价钱",
            "text": "相差 16 - 7 = 9 件 T 恤，钱数相差 $8 + $19 = $27。于是 9 件共 $27，每件是 $3。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求 2 个答案",
            "text": "2 件 T 恤的价钱是 2 × $3 = $6。Cleo 原有 7 × $3 + $19 = $40。"
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "验算：(a) $6；(b) $40"
      }
    },
