    "question": "Carol spent 30% of her money on 3 blouses and 2 skirts costing $288 altogether. Each blouse cost 2/5 as much as a skirt. (a) How much money did she have at 1st? (b) How much more did a skirt cost than a blouse?",
    "answer": "(a) $960; (b) $54",
    "model": "money-units",
    "hint": "Represent 1 blouse as 2 units and 1 skirt as 5 units. The 3 blouses and 2 skirts form 16 units worth $288.",
    "solution": {
      "en": {
        "strategy": "Turn the blouse-to-skirt price relationship into ratio units, then use the 30% spending statement.",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "Build price units",
            "text": "A blouse costs 2/5 as much as a skirt, so use 2 units for 1 blouse and 5 units for 1 skirt. The 3 blouses and 2 skirts cost 3 × 2 + 2 × 5 = 16 units."
          },
          {
            "title": "Find each clothing price",
            "text": "16 units cost $288, so 1 unit costs $288 ÷ 16 = $18. A blouse costs 2 × $18 = $36 and a skirt costs 5 × $18 = $90."
          },
          {
            "title": "Find the original money",
            "text": "$288 was 30% of Carol's money, so her original amount was $288 ÷ 30% = $960. The skirt cost $90 - $36 = $54 more than the blouse."
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "Check: (a) $960; (b) $54"
      },
      "zh-Hans": {
        "strategy": "把衬衫和裙子的价格关系化成份数，再使用 30% 的条件。",
        "steps": [
          {
            "title": "建立价格份数",
            "text": "衬衫价格是裙子的 2/5，所以 1 件衬衫用 2 份表示，1 条裙子用 5 份表示。3 件衬衫和 2 条裙子共 3 × 2 + 2 × 5 = 16 份。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求每件衣服价格",
            "text": "16 份共 $288，所以 1 份是 $288 ÷ 16 = $18。衬衫是 2 × $18 = $36，裙子是 5 × $18 = $90。"
          },
          {
            "title": "求原有钱数",
            "text": "$288 是 Carol 钱数的 30%，所以原有 $288 ÷ 30% = $960。裙子比衬衫贵 $90 - $36 = $54。"
          }
        ],
        "answerCheck": "验算：(a) $960；(b) $54"
      }
    },
